  "problem_statement": "feat: self-improvement — Reflexion + auto-skill authoring\n\nTwo closed loops that make Wells get better at a repo the more it's used.\n\nReflexion (#1): after a run that failed the test gate or was rejected by\nthe reviewer, the finisher writes a structured critique to\n.wells/reflections.md (deduped by signature, size-capped). The planner\nretrieves the top-K reflections relevant to the current goal and injects\nthem, so the same failure mode isn't repeated across runs. Keyword-overlap\nranking by default (deterministic, free); opt-in embedding re-rank.\n\nAuto-skill authoring (#2): after a clean, verified run, the finisher\npackages the proven plan into a SKILL.md proposal staged under\n.wells/skill-proposals/. Proposals cost zero context (not scanned by the\nskills system) until the user accepts them via /skills proposals, which\npromotes them to .wells/skills/<name>/SKILL.md (a new discoverable root).\n\nThree notification surfaces ensure proposed skills are noticed: an\nend-of-run panel (every surface), a clickable right-panel banner (TUI),\nand a ProposalReviewScreen modal (list/view/accept/reject/edit-then-accept).\n\nBoth features default on, degrade to no-ops when disabled, and honour the\nsafety gate. 1003 tests pass.",
